    {
      "id": "antony-and-cleopatra/sceneIV_3.6/p@160989",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "ENOBARBUS.\nAlexas did revolt and went to Jewry on\nAffairs of Antony; there did dissuade\nGreat Herod to incline himself to Caesar\nAnd leave his master Antony. For this pains\nCaesar hath hanged him. Canidius and the rest\nThat fell away have entertainment but\nNo honourable trust. I have done ill,\nOf which I do accuse myself so sorely\nThat I will joy no more.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
